{\pard\sb360\sa120\keepn\b Record protocol \u183? formal theory \u183? version formal-0.4\par}
{\pard\sa160 Published object 1 (appendix D.1). What a research record in the formal-theory modality contains, how its parts point at each other, and what the Level 2 checks mean for it. The protocol is a field specification: it belongs to the field, not to one journal. Findings cite its clauses as {\f1 protocol/formal.md#P<n>}.\par}
{\pard\sb240\sa120\keepn\b P1. The record's parts\par}
{\pard\sa160 A record is a folder with a manifest, {\f1 record.yaml} (schema {\f1 schemas/record.schema.yaml}), and these parts:\par}
