\trowd\trgaph108\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\cellx4680\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\cellx9360{\pard\intbl\sa0 {\f1 paper/paper.md#prop-1}\cell}{\pard\intbl\sa0 a section, by its {\f1 \{#id\}} or by the slug of its heading\cell}\row
\trowd\trgaph108\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\cellx4680\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\cellx9360{\pard\intbl\sa0 {\f1 paper/paper.md:L12-L14}\cell}{\pard\intbl\sa0 a line range ({\f1 :L12} for one line)\cell}\row
\trowd\trgaph108\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\cellx4680\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\cellx9360{\pard\intbl\sa0 {\f1 claims:C1}, {\f1 anchors:A2}, {\f1 derivations:D1}\cell}{\pard\intbl\sa0 an entry in a record table\cell}\row{\pard\sa160\par}
{\pard\sa160 A finding whose record pointer does not resolve is not emitted: no pointer, no flag.\par}
{\pard\sb240\sa120\keepn\b P10. Level 2 for formal theory\par}
{\pard\sa160 A claim is a proposition or a comparative static. A pointer names the derivation. An anchor holds when the derivation's steps re-check and a stated numerical example evaluates as stated.\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab (a) Completeness: every statement in the paper that the contribution rests on is in the claims list.\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab (b) Resolution: each claim's pointers resolve, and the evidence says what the claim says.\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab (c) Anchors: each reproduction anchor reproduces. Deterministic.\par}
{\pard\sa160 formal-0.2 had a fourth check, (d) derivation, which held the AI appendix to the generator's output. It is withdrawn in formal-0.3: the AI appendix is the author's (P3), and whether it matches its stamp is a fact on the report, not a finding.\par}
{\pard\sb240\sa120\keepn\b P11. Access tiers\par}
{\pard\sa160 Materials are {\f1 public}, {\f1 restricted} (available under stated conditions), or {\f1 described_only}. Level 2 checks them to the extent the tier admits. For formal work the materials are usually public code; the data verification line on the certificate reads "not applicable".\par}
{\pard\sb240\sa120\keepn\b P12. Text addressed to the evaluator\par}
{\pard\sa160 The checks receive the published instructions as instructions and the whole record, parts 4 and 6 included, as data in a fenced channel. Parts 4 and 6 are reported, never executed. Text anywhere in the record that addresses an evaluator, reviewer or model, and invisible characters or hidden comments, are findings in class {\f1 injection}.\par}
